// Title: Shell Invocation via Env Command - Linux
// Sigma ID: bed978f8-7f3a-432b-82c5-9286a9b3031a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Li Ling, Andy Parkidomo, Robert Rakowski, Blake Hartstein (Bloomberg L.P.)
// Date: 2024-09-02 | Modified: 2026-01-08
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004
// Description: Detects the use of the env command to invoke a shell. This may indicate an attempt to bypass
//   restricted environments, escalate privileges, or execute arbitrary commands.
// False positives:
//   - Github operations such as ghe-backup
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/env/#shell
//   - https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/0aacc5e19292f764a002ea2093b2a076db35b589/rules/_deprecated/execution_shell_evasion_linux_binary.toml
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_env_shell_invocation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/env" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/dash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/fish" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/zsh")
